WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.169 --> 00:00:10.570
In this part of level editing I want to talk about HLOD or hierarchical level of detail generation for our landscape.

2
00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:19.199
Now this option can be found by simply selecting our landscape and then under the HLOD sections in the details panel

3
00:00:19.199 --> 00:00:25.000
we'll find our HLOD texture size policy and HLOD texture size.

4
00:00:25.039 --> 00:00:34.399
Now setting the HLOD texture size policy to specific size allows us to define the size of the resulting texture

5
00:00:34.399 --> 00:00:39.159
that will be generated and applied to our landscape for our level of detail.

6
00:00:39.159 --> 00:00:43.399
And we can see an example of this in our slides in front of us.

7
00:00:43.399 --> 00:00:48.600
At the top we have this set to 256 and at the bottom we have it set to 4096.

8
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:55.399
So notice that the 4096 one does have more detail in it but one other thing to take into consideration.

9
00:00:55.399 --> 00:00:59.000
This texture is meant to be seen at a very very far distance.

10
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.920
So while 4096 does show some better detail oftentimes this is not going to be needed.

11
00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:13.079
The other thing about generating a texture this large as your landscape grows in complexity and in size

12
00:01:13.079 --> 00:01:15.560
it can take a very long time to generate this texture.

13
00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:22.840
Not to mention a texture of 4096 for your entire landscape is going to take up a lot of disk space as well as memory space.

14
00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:25.799
Let's take a look at how we can quickly do this in the editor.

15
00:01:25.799 --> 00:01:32.920
So first things first if you notice I don't actually have anything to see if I was to come here to my landscape and actually hide it.

16
00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:38.200
I can't actually see my HLOD so in order to see that what we do if we come up here to show

17
00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:44.840
we can come down to HLOD and then show our HLODs and this will allow us right here if we just pop that over like so.

18
00:01:45.159 --> 00:01:54.519
Now what we're going to see here is this is our HLOD asset and if I was to come back here and unhide this this is our landscape.

19
00:01:54.519 --> 00:02:00.680
So let's click on our landscape now that we can see the HLOD results and we're going to come down here to our HLOD section.

20
00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:06.120
You can see here I have again my HLOD texture size policy and my HLOD texture size.

21
00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:13.879
So 128 let's set this to something like 64 and then let's just come up here to build and we're going to build HLODs.

22
00:02:13.879 --> 00:02:19.159
We're going to say build HLODs we're going to go ahead and save this and we'll be right back once this finishes building.

23
00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:24.150
All right now that we are back inside of the editor let's come up here to our landscape.

24
00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:29.189
We're just going to hide this really quick and that is our HLOD result right there.

25
00:02:29.189 --> 00:02:34.229
Now it is got you know it's got some issues right here and there but remember this is

26
00:02:34.229 --> 00:02:40.870
generally going to be somewhere seeing something from like this far away so those little issues might not be that apparent.

27
00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:47.990
However if they are simply just come here to our settings we'll set this back to 128 and come back to build and we will build this.

28
00:02:49.849 --> 00:02:57.669
And you can see it's just going to be that easy to rebuild our HLODs for this landscape.

29
00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:03.509
And with a little movie magic we now have this new version of our landscape.

30
00:03:03.509 --> 00:03:05.270
Let's go ahead and just hide that again real quick.

31
00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:11.110
There we go boom it has been updated you can see it does have a little bit more resolution inside of it.

32
00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:14.710
Things are just a little bit sharper but again remember we're looking at things

33
00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:18.969
off here in the distance so that is a really fantastic result.

34
00:03:18.969 --> 00:03:21.530
Remember again we find this by coming to our landscape.

35
00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:27.289
And then underneath our details panel HLOD and setting our HLOD texture size.
